From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:02:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: stop declaring a HIDL fingerprint sensor

config_biometric_sensors dates from when this device ran a HIDL
fingerprint HAL. It has shipped the AIDL one
(android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint-service.lineage, declared in
VINTF as IFingerprint/default v4) for a long time, and the overlay was
never removed.

AuthService reads that array as the list of *HIDL* sensors:

  getFingerprintConfiguration -> getConfiguration
      -> config_biometric_sensors
  new FingerprintSensorConfigurations(
      !(hidlConfigStrings != null && hidlConfigStrings.length > 0))

so a non-empty list means resetLockoutRequiresHardwareAuthToken=false,
FingerprintProvider takes its "Adding HIDL configs" branch, and every
sensor is wrapped in a HidlToAidlSensorAdapter. Its isHardwareDetected
calls IBiometricsFingerprint.getService(), which this device has no
HAL for:

  hwservicemanager: Cannot find entry
      android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint@2.1::IBiometricsFingerprint
  BiometricEnrollActivity: Unexpected result (has enrollments): 1

1 is BIOMETRIC_ERROR_HW_UNAVAILABLE, so BiometricEnrollActivity finishes
immediately and Settings offers no fingerprint entry at all. Everything
underneath looks healthy -- HAL running, IFingerprint/default
registered, sensor 0 at strength 15, zero HAL deaths -- which is what
made this hard to see.
---
 .../base/core/res/res/values/config.xml       | 20 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
index 6a300b05..7b3238cc 100644
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -195,14 +195,18 @@
     <!-- Minimum color temperature, in Kelvin, supported by Night display. -->
     <integer name="config_nightDisplayColorTemperatureMin">1200</integer>
 
-    <!-- List of biometric sensors on the device, in decreasing strength. Consumed by AuthService
-         when registering authenticators with BiometricService. Format must be ID:Modality:Strength,
-         where: IDs are unique per device, Modality as defined in BiometricAuthenticator.java,
-         and Strength as defined in Authenticators.java -->
-    <string-array name="config_biometric_sensors" translatable="false">
-        <!-- ID0:Fingerprint:Strong -->
-        <item>0:2:15</item>
-    </string-array>
+    <!-- config_biometric_sensors is deliberately NOT set. AuthService reads it as the list of
+         *HIDL* sensors (getFingerprintConfiguration -> getConfiguration -> config_biometric_sensors),
+         and a non-empty list makes it construct FingerprintSensorConfigurations with
+         resetLockoutRequiresHardwareAuthToken=false. FingerprintProvider then takes the "Adding HIDL
+         configs" branch and wraps every sensor in a HidlToAidlSensorAdapter, whose isHardwareDetected
+         calls IBiometricsFingerprint.getService() -- a HIDL HAL this device has not shipped since it
+         moved to android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint-service.lineage (AIDL, declared in VINTF).
+         The lookup fails, canAuthenticate returns BIOMETRIC_ERROR_HW_UNAVAILABLE, and Settings hides
+         fingerprint enrolment entirely with no error the user can see.
+
+         With it absent, the AIDL instance is used, sensor strength comes from the HAL's own
+         SensorProps, and the authenticator still registers with BiometricService. -->
 
     <!-- The list of components which should be automatically disabled for a specific device. -->
     <string-array name="config_deviceDisabledComponents" translatable="false">
